			"originalText": "Scale Mathematics",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
		{
			"id": "xWXtCZit",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -357.4647610162227,
			"y": 2799.2918707405,
			"width": 815.4924567618037,
			"height": 476.93371544217473,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b1L",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1273629896,
			"version": 110,
			"versionNonce": 1125002440,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": null,
			"updated": 1783698074155,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Bloom filter size depends on 3 things:\n\nn = number of items you're storing (e.g., 2 billion Gmail addresses)\np = how many false positives you're okay with (e.g., 1%)\nFrom n and p, you calculate:\n\nm = size of bit array\nk = number of hash functions\n\n\n\nFormulas (don't worry, just for intuition):\n\nm = -(n * ln(p)) / (ln(2)^2)\nk = (m/n) * ln(2)",
			"rawText": "Bloom filter size depends on 3 things:\n\nn = number of items you're storing (e.g., 2 billion Gmail addresses)\np = how many false positives you're okay with (e.g., 1%)\nFrom n and p, you calculate:\n\nm = size of bit array\nk = number of hash functions\n\n\n\nFormulas (don't worry, just for intuition):\n\nm = -(n * ln(p)) / (ln(2)^2)\nk = (m/n) * ln(2)",
			"fontSize": 25.436464823582657,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Bloom filter size depends on 3 things:\n\nn = number of items you're storing (e.g., 2 billion Gmail addresses)\np = how many false positives you're okay with (e.g., 1%)\nFrom n and p, you calculate:\n\nm = size of bit array\nk = number of hash functions\n\n\n\nFormulas (don't worry, just for intuition):\n\nm = -(n * ln(p)) / (ln(2)^2)\nk = (m/n) * ln(2)",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
		{
			"id": "TKJxuPRx",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -402.6245248265966,
			"y": 3329.6782082177383,
			"width": 239.47982094183237,
			"height": 47.591407068716755,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b1M",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1639002056,
			"version": 41,
			"versionNonce": 362064568,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": null,
			"updated": 1783698112180,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Real Example",
			"rawText": "Real Example",
			"fontSize": 38.07312565497338,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Real Example",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
		{
			"id": "Ie9YbTuC",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -365.82063363668163,
			"y": 3422.585427858847,
			"width": 1404.125803512572,
			"height": 205.3468661880189,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b1N",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1987570376,
			"version": 114,
			"versionNonce": 1962913224,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": null,
			"updated": 1783698120256,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Example: For 1 billion items with 1% false positive rate:\n\nYou'd need roughly ~9.6 bits per item → about 1.2 GB total for the whole bit array.\nNumber of hash functions k ≈ 7.\n\nCompare that to storing 1 billion actual email strings (avg 20 bytes each) = 20 GB+. Bloom filter is more than 15x smaller.\nThis is why it scales — you can hold \"does this exist\" info for billions of items using just a few GB of RAM.",
			"rawText": "Example: For 1 billion items with 1% false positive rate:\n\nYou'd need roughly ~9.6 bits per item → about 1.2 GB total for the whole bit array.\nNumber of hash functions k ≈ 7.\n\nCompare that to storing 1 billion actual email strings (avg 20 bytes each) = 20 GB+. Bloom filter is more than 15x smaller.\nThis is why it scales — you can hold \"does this exist\" info for billions of items using just a few GB of RAM.",
			"fontSize": 23.46821327863074,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Example: For 1 billion items with 1% false positive rate:\n\nYou'd need roughly ~9.6 bits per item → about 1.2 GB total for the whole bit array.\nNumber of hash functions k ≈ 7.\n\nCompare that to storing 1 billion actual email strings (avg 20 bytes each) = 20 GB+. Bloom filter is more than 15x smaller.\nThis is why it scales — you can hold \"does this exist\" info for billions of items using just a few GB of RAM.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false
		},
